From 627980e17c3977875cbc11966e448057f2b8c67a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:46:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision output (this video): applied while it plays, for
 HDR10 and HDR10+ too, kept for each file

"Dolby Vision output (this video)" (the video settings of the player,
PlayerControl(HadesDVOutput)) did nothing since Kodi's "Don't reopen a
stream if it is already selected" (Piers, ec5c73f): the choice asks for
the video stream that plays, and VideoPlayer opens it again only when it
is another one. The choice was kept, and the video went on as before
(issue #6; asked for in the LibreELEC thread).

- VideoPlayer remembers the choice its video stream was opened with
  (m_dvChoiceOpened) and opens that same stream again when the choice now
  differs (DVChoiceChanged()), at the time it is at, as another video
  stream would be: close, open, accurate seek back. An add-on that selects
  the stream that plays still opens nothing again. The picture and the
  sound stop for about as long as a seek; where the output changes, the TV
  changes its picture mode. kodi.log: "the output chosen for this video is
  taken: its video stream is opened again, and playback goes back to N ms".
- The choice is also offered for an HDR10 video (as the settings say,
  Dolby Vision measured from the picture, or as Kodi plays it) and for an
  HDR10+ one (as the settings say, Dolby Vision made from its HDR10+
  metadata, also on a display that takes HDR10+, or as Kodi plays it),
  where the display takes native Dolby Vision (ChoiceSource,
  ChoiceOffered()). What makes such a stream Dolby Vision is the demuxer,
  which now follows the choice (CDVDDemux::DVOutputChoiceChanged()): a
  stream it made Dolby Vision is given back where the choice says no, and
  one it left as it was is looked at again where it says yes. The
  settings of each format stay what decides by default: nothing is
  written to them.
- The choice is kept for the file and taken again when it plays next
  (DVBRIDGE::FileOpened(), KeepOutputChoice()); "as the settings say"
  forgets it. Files are kept by the SHA-256 of their path, never by name,
  in special://profile/hades-dv-output.txt (the last 1000; written
  through a temporary file). A kept choice holds only where it is offered
  for what the video stream turns out to be and can be had now
  (KeptChoiceHolds(), checked in VideoStreamOpened()); otherwise the video
  plays as the settings say, and kodi.log says so. Kodi's video database
  is not touched.

One string (core #39828, Estuary #32240 with es_es, es_mx and es_ar).
Test (host): ChoiceSourceOf(), ChoiceOffered(), KeptChoiceHolds(),
Hdr10AsDolbyVisionFor(), DOLBY_VISION in the rules of a stream, and the
memory of each file (103 checks; six mutations caught). Not run on a
display: the reopening, the demuxer giving a stream back or making it
Dolby Vision mid-file, the HDMI changes that follow.
